1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nc6 (2... d6 3. Nf3 (3. d4 exd4 4. Qxd4 Nc6 {[%csl Od6]} 5. Qd3 Nf6 6. Bf4 $14) 3... Nf6 4. d4 {Transposing into a Philidor.}) 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d3 Be7 (4... d6 5. f4 Be7 (5... Bg4 6. Nge2) 6. Nf3 Bg4 (6... O-O 7. f5 $14 {We can play in the spirit of the Bc5 line here.}) 7. h3 Bxf3 8. Qxf3 Nd4 9. Qf2 c6 10. a4 O-O 11. O-O $36 {1-0 Costachi,M (2464)-Tusu,N (1894) Bucharest ROM GP 2025 (2)}) (4... h6 5. f4 $36 {1-0 Ponkratov,P (2632)-Petrosyan,M (2613) Wch Blitz Moscow 2019 (6)}) 5. a3 {[%csl Ba3,Yc4]} (5. f4 {Black hasn't played d6 yet, so d5 is an option.} exf4 6. Bxf4 O-O 7. Nf3 Na5 {to take the bishop.} 8. Bb3 Nxb3 9. axb3 d5 $132 {And it's absolutely fine for Black.}) 5... O-O 6. Nge2 d6 7. O-O {[%cal Gf2f4] Only now do we think about f4.} Be6 8. Nd5 Nb8 (8... Bxd5 9. exd5 Nb8 10. Ng3 $14 {[%cal Gf2f4,Gg3f5];1-0 Kitchlew,A-Taylor,R Guernsey Holiday op 2001 (5)}) 9. Ng3 (9. a4 c6 10. Nxe7+ Qxe7 11. Ng3 $14) 9... Nxd5 10. exd5 Bc8 11. d4 $14 {Nabaty played f4, but I think that White is slightly better, so clearly the opening was successful.} (11. f4 Nd7 12. Qf3 f5 13. Ne2 Bf6 14. Bd2 exf4 15. d4 g5 16. h4 h6 17. g3 Bg7 18. hxg5 hxg5 19. gxf4 g4 20. Qb3 Rf6 21. Kg2 Rh6 22. Rh1 Nf8 23. Rxh6 Bxh6 24. Rh1 Bg7 25. Ng3 Ng6 26. Rh5 Nh4+ 27. Kf2 Bf6 28. Bd3 Qe8 29. c3 Nf3 30. Bxf5 Bxf5 31. Rxf5 Bh4 32. Qc2 Bxg3+ 33. Kxg3 Qe2 34. Rh5 {1-0 Nabaty,T (2647)-Postny,E (2605) Jerusalem Israel op 2019 (5)}) *

