n the kingside. 0.00 is the evaluation, but it's a new and very playable position.} (12. O-O-O $2 Bxc3 13. Qxc3 Nxe4 $1 $19 {[%csl Be4,Rg5] Bg5 is hanging.})) 10. Bxf6 Qxf6 11. Nd5 $1 Qg6 $1 {[%csl Re4,Rg2] important counterplay against e4.} (11... Qd8 $6 12. O-O $16 {[%csl Bd4,Be4][%cal Gc2c3] c3 next, and White is positionally better.}) 12. O-O Qxe4 $1 {Black must take the pawn; otherwise, his position is just worse.} (12... Bg4 {less precise.} 13. c3 Qxe4 14. Qd2 $36 {[%cal Ga1e1]}) 13. c3 {[%csl Bc3,Yd4] we should consolidate the d4 pawn.} Be6 $1 {[%csl Rd5] the best because it's direct.} (13... Bg4 14. Qd2 $36 {[%cal Ga1e1]}) 14. Nd2 $1 Qh4 $1 {[%csl Bh4]} (14... Qg6 $2 15. Nf4 $16 {[%csl Re6,Rg6]}) 15. Rf4 Qd8 $1 (15... Qg5 $2 16. h4 Qd8 17. Nxb6 axb6 18. d5 $18 {[%csl Bh4][%cal Rd8g5] Black doesn't have the key Qg5 resource.}) 16. Nf6+ $5 (16. Nxb6 $2 {we don't win material because of} axb6 17. d5 Qg5 $19 {[%csl Bg5] key resource.}) (16. Ne4 f5 $1 {[%csl Bf5]} 17. Qe2 $5 (17. Ng3 Bxd5 18. Bxd5+ Kh8 $11 {[%cal Gf4f5] we can take back on f5, but it will be very little.}) 17... Bxd5 18. Bxd5+ Kh8 19. Raf1 $36) 16... Kh8 (16... gxf6 $4 17. Qh5 $18 {[%csl Rg8]}) 17. Qh5 Ne5 $1 (17... Ne7 18. Raf1 $1 d5 19. Bd3 $40 {[%csl Rh8]}) (17... d5 18. Nxd5 Bxd5 19. Qxd5 Qxd5 20. Bxd5 Nxd4 $1 21. cxd4 Rad8 22. Bxb7 Bxd4+ 23. Rxd4 (23. Kf1 $2 Be3 $15 {[%csl Rd2,Rf4]}) 23... Rxd4 24. Nb3 $14 {[%csl Ra7,Bb3,Rc7]}) 18. Raf1 (18. b3 $5 $13) (18. Bxe6 fxe6 19. Raf1 Qe7 $1 20. Nde4 Qf7 21. Ne8 Qxh5 22. Rxf8+ Kh7 23. N4f6+ gxf6 24. Nxf6+ Kg6 25. Rxa8 Qe2 $1 26. Rf8 $5 $13) 18... Bxc4 {[%csl Bc4]} (18... Nxc4 $4 19. Rh4 $18 {[%cal Gh5g5] g5 next and mate is coming.}) 19. Nxc4 Nxc4 20. Qh3 {[%cal Gf4h4,Gh4h6] Rh4 next and we are ready for mate.} Rg8 $1 {only move.} 21. Rf5 $5 {[%cal Gf6g4,Rd8g5] with the idea Ng4, where Black won't have Qg5.} (21. Rh4 $2 gxf6 22. Rxh6+ Kg7 $17 {[%cal Gg7f8]}) (21. Ng4 Qg5 22. Rf5 Qg6 23. Rh5 $13) 21... Qe7 22. Ng4 $36 *

